1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,301
This is Credentia, running live on Monad testnet.

2
00:00:04,301 --> 00:00:09,816
An issuer creates a credential, and anyone can verify it from a link, with nothing to install

3
00:00:09,816 --> 00:00:10,910
and no account.

4
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:13,311
The site walks you through it.

5
00:00:13,311 --> 00:00:16,526
Issue a credential, share the link or the QR code,

6
00:00:16,526 --> 00:00:18,650
and anyone can check it instantly.

7
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:20,913
Issuing starts here.

8
00:00:20,913 --> 00:00:25,165
The form asks for a title, a recipient, their wallet address,

9
00:00:25,165 --> 00:00:26,851
and an optional expiry.

10
00:00:26,851 --> 00:00:28,910
It checks each field as you go,

11
00:00:28,910 --> 00:00:31,570
so a malformed address is caught straight away.

12
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:34,571
Issuing is for authorised issuers.

13
00:00:34,571 --> 00:00:39,454
The page asks them to sign in with a passkey, and the registry only accepts issuers

14
00:00:39,454 --> 00:00:41,667
that pass our testnet identity gate.

15
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:44,346
That gate is a stand-in for a real verifier,

16
00:00:44,346 --> 00:00:45,750
and the page says so.

17
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:48,193
Now the verifier's side.

18
00:00:48,193 --> 00:00:51,743
This is a real credential, issued on Monad testnet.

19
00:00:51,743 --> 00:00:54,641
Opening its link reads the registry directly.

20
00:00:54,641 --> 00:00:56,410
No account, no wallet.

21
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:59,044
The page shows four checks.

22
00:00:59,044 --> 00:01:05,082
The link was read, the credential exists in the registry, the details match the on-chain fingerprint,

23
00:01:05,082 --> 00:01:06,280
and it's still active.

24
00:01:07,010 --> 00:01:12,226
It shows who issued it, and the verify button opens the transaction on the Monad explorer,

25
00:01:12,226 --> 00:01:14,840
so anyone can confirm it independently.

26
00:01:15,570 --> 00:01:22,043
Every credential also has a receipt: its status, ID, issuer, the transaction hash,

27
00:01:22,043 --> 00:01:23,090
and the network.

28
00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:27,920
Now change one detail in the link, here, the recipient name.

29
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:31,872
The fingerprint no longer matches,

30
00:01:31,872 --> 00:01:35,100
and Credentia tells the verifier not to rely on it.

31
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:38,523
And when an issuer withdraws a credential,

32
00:01:38,523 --> 00:01:40,030
the page says revoked.

33
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:43,567
In our local setup, an Envio indexer turns

34
00:01:43,567 --> 00:01:46,219
the registry's events into a timeline.

35
00:01:46,219 --> 00:01:48,900
The credential was issued, then revoked.

36
00:01:49,630 --> 00:01:51,350
That's Credentia.

37
00:01:51,350 --> 00:01:55,832
A credential anyone can verify, and nobody can quietly edit.

38
00:01:55,832 --> 00:01:57,857
Live on Monad testnet today,

39
00:01:57,857 --> 00:01:59,920
with the demo data labelled as such.
